    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7faddb67_d16ce837",
        "filename": "doc/source/admin/configure_tokenless_x509.rst",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 8482
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-10T01:56:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As an operator, especially one not super familiar with X.509, it\u0027s confusing to see references to the issue intermixed with references to the client cert. It would be helpful to be really explicit about which is which, maybe even with a short example of how you might create a client cert given an existing issuer cert.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 128,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "9f1abd4364b163471297a23192305ecc7fec7cda",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7faddb67_fe251aac",
        "filename": "doc/source/admin/configure_tokenless_x509.rst",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 1916
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-11T00:37:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be difficult for operators to use this feature if they don\u0027t have a basic understanding of SSL and certificates. There are a lot of examples out there on how to generate a PKI already. I don\u0027t think we should go too deep in to educating people on what PKI and certificates are. Perhaps we can suggest them to read the OpenSSL book as a prereq?",
      "parentUuid": "7faddb67_d16ce837",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 128,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "9f1abd4364b163471297a23192305ecc7fec7cda",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
